# Real configuration. The Firebase web keys in here are not secrets — they ship
# in the client bundle either way, and what protects the data is firestore.rules
# and database.rules.json. This is ignored because it points at *our* project and
# nobody else's checkout should.
.env
.env.local

# Security rules with the two real addresses filled in, generated by
# `npm run rules`. The templates beside them are the version to keep.
rules-out

